  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Impact Cluster: Livestock Transformation Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to develop a scalable model (concept) for location-fixed dairy farming to contribute to improving the position of Fulani dairy producers by initiating a process of domesticating cows on a farm and modernising the market for meats, dairy and related processed parts in Nigeria. The project in Nasarawe State will deliver results and impact in terms of:&#x2022;	Establishing the proof of concept for developing the market for beef and dairy production by Fulani farmers/herders to serve the Federal Capital Territory (FCT) Abuja and environs market. The proposed pilot farm will be based in Nasarawe State and intended to produce output for sale to buyers in Abuja, Nigeria&#x2019;s capital city with a population of around 3.1 million persons.&#x2022;	Capital Spend Focus: milk processing, meat processing (abattoirs), and the necessary infrastructure e.g. competitive electricity, and forage and water supply.&#x2022;	Demonstrating an alternative and attractive new way of dairy farming (and life) that secures the development of the livestock sector in the future.&#x2022;	Enhancing the process of knowledge development. A Training-of-trainers programme is arranged to secure future knowledge transfer. Coaching the farm managers group of the demonstration farm is also part of securing knowledge.&#x2022;	The masterplan produced by the consortium for the future rollout of the Nigerian Livestock Transformation Impact Cluster (NLTP) in Nigeria will open the market for future Dutch business and investments in Nigeria.The NLTP will stimulate and facilitate the change of this pastoralist way of farming to a more manageable sustainable way of life with better quality for humans and animals. The NLTP will be the basics to build the infrastructure of the cattle sector with a positive net impact on the economy.</narrative>
  </description>
